1
00:00:03,068 --> 00:00:05,491
This morning, the sea touched the rocks.

2
00:00:05,541 --> 00:00:07,656
Tonight, it has gone far, far away:

3
00:00:07,706 --> 00:00:09,634
the boat is sitting on the sand!

4
00:00:09,684 --> 00:00:11,045
Where does the sea go?

5
00:00:11,889 --> 00:00:13,895
The next morning: it's back!

6
00:00:13,945 --> 00:00:16,611
The sea rises and falls, twice a day.

7
00:00:16,661 --> 00:00:18,277
But who is pulling it?

8
00:00:19,052 --> 00:00:20,566
Discovery mission!

9
00:00:23,082 --> 00:00:23,657
Mini mode!

10
00:00:23,707 --> 00:00:26,032
The Moon pulls on everything on Earth,

11
00:00:26,082 --> 00:00:26,907
just a little.

12
00:00:26,957 --> 00:00:29,282
Rocks don't move, but water can slide:

13
00:00:29,332 --> 00:00:31,645
on the Moon's side, it makes a bulge.

14
00:00:32,410 --> 00:00:34,608
And on the other side of the Earth?

15
00:00:34,658 --> 00:00:36,213
The Moon pulls less hard:

16
00:00:36,263 --> 00:00:38,076
the water stays a bit behind.

17
00:00:38,126 --> 00:00:39,089
A second bulge!

18
00:00:41,428 --> 00:00:44,989
Meanwhile, the Earth turns beneath the two bulges.

19
00:00:45,039 --> 00:00:48,094
Your beach passes under a bulge: high tide!

20
00:00:48,144 --> 00:00:49,971
Between the two: low tide.

21
00:00:50,021 --> 00:00:50,888
Twice a day.

22
00:00:51,664 --> 00:00:52,998
Look: the Moon is rising,

23
00:00:53,048 --> 00:00:54,492
and the sea is coming back.

24
00:00:54,542 --> 00:00:56,595
Even in daytime, when we can't see it,

25
00:00:56,645 --> 00:00:58,803
the Moon is still pulling on the water.

26
00:00:59,612 --> 00:01:01,641
That's why the sea rises and falls.

27
00:01:03,139 --> 00:01:04,879
The Moon pulls on the ocean's water:

28
00:01:04,929 --> 00:01:07,614
two bulges of water, and the Earth turns beneath them.

29
00:01:09,098 --> 00:01:10,941
With an adult, at the beach:

30
00:01:10,991 --> 00:01:13,375
plant a stick where the sea reaches.

31
00:01:13,425 --> 00:01:15,944
Come back an hour later: it has moved!

32
00:01:15,994 --> 00:01:17,210
Rising or falling?

33
00:01:18,012 --> 00:01:20,374
And why does the ground sometimes shake?

34
00:01:20,424 --> 00:01:21,630
The answer tomorrow.
